WEBVTT

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.210
What was that shock?

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.180
An explosion on the outside of the ship!

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.190
Where did the explosion happen?

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:25.690
I'll check!

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.140
A coupler for the gravity control system's damaged!

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.490
Is it having any effect on the inside of the ship?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.860
We're fine.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:39.150
This is bad! It's become impossible to release the gravity control unit!

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:40.130
What?

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.360
That's impossible!

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.280
Can we fix it with the drones?

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.960
No! The gravitational field outside is too chaotic!

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.340
It's impossible for the drones.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.050
What's wrong? What happened?

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.200
At this rate we won't be able to release the gravity control unit.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.630
What's going to happen?

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.060
I don't want to think about it...

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.950
...but even I know what that means.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.300
To where everyone is.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.650
I'll go by myself. Everyone, get off the ship.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.230
What do you plan to accomplish by going alone?

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.230
Crash the ship into the gravity storm.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.820
That's too reckless!

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.140
There isn't any other way.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:25.200
Idiot! You're the one who said we weren't going so we could die, weren't you Kaoru?

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.190
I'll go!

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.580
Kaoru, you take everyone and go back to the planet.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.330
It's impossible for you to pilot, Bell!

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.550
They need you to pilot the escape shuttle, Kaoru!

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.290
Just give me orders by radio!

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.800
Wait! Don't decide this for yourself!

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.110
If you're going, I'm going too!

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:42.830
That's right!

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.100
We'll all go!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.230
But...

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:45.860
Kaoru...

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:47.400
It's pointless.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.680
No matter what you say, the rest of our feelings won't change.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.140
How much time do you think we've spend together?

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:02.510
Through painful times and sad times, we overcame them all together!

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.340
The sadness of losing one of our friends would be too painful to bear.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:10.350
So don't think that way again!

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.910
We can't allow you to go by yourself!

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.280
It's dangerous! Everyone take your seats and fasten your seat belts!

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.780
Survive, are you ready?

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:43.610
It seems this will be my final act in fulfilling my duty.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:47.180
The gravity storm's affect is causing more disturbances!

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.310
Everyone, I'm sorry.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.540
From here on, Survive and I will go alone.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.510
What did you say?

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:54.620
With Survive?

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:55.990
What do you mean?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:58.390
Kaoru, I'm counting on you.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.580
Everyone, brace yourselves for the jet blast.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.540
Wait! What you sayin'?

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.530
I can't remove the belt!

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.730
Launch in five seconds!

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.550
Three... two... one...

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:29.030
Luna!

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:33.370
Idiot! Weren't we always gonna be together?

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:34.950
Luna...

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.040
Luna, what are you planning to do?

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.260
What you were planning to do alone, Kaoru.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:52.390
You mean crash the ship into the gravity storm?

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:58.480
I don't how well it will work, but I'll definitely try.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:04.130
Idiot! We said if anyone was going, we were all going!

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.130
Howard... thank you.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.490
Why did you decide for yourself?

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.590
There wasn't enough time.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.130
Sorry, Menori.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.150
Take care of everyone.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:17.180
It's no use!

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.660
I can't let you act on your own!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.090
Once you've used the gravity control unit, will you be able to get back?

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.360
I'll take any and every chance I get. Thanks, Shingo.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.730
Luna! Don't forget what I'm about to tell you!

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:41.140
No matter what happens, don't give up!

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:45.340
Thanks, Bell. I won't give up.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.190
Luna, I couldn't bear it if you died!

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.260
Come back! Make sure you come back!

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.330
Thanks, Sharla.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:55.990
We'll definitely see each other again.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.680
It's a promise.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.950
I'll wait... however long as it takes.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:06.380
Luna, why'd you leave me behind?

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.860
You tryin' to leave me all alone again?

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.730
You're not alone anymore, Chako. You have everyone now.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:15.860
Yeah, but...

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.880
Chako, I won't forget those words.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.450
When something bad happens, look up at the sky!

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.340
You can't brood over it forever.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.290
In your heart, there's always...

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.330
...a blue sky.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:36.830
I don't want you to!

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.530
Don't go, Luna!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:40.840
Luna!

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.610
Thanks, Adam, Tako.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.310
All of you, shape this planet's future.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:49.160
Luna!

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.710
Everyone, off I go!

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.400
We'll be waiting for you.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.360
Make sure you come back!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.050
Luna...

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:28.340
Transfer all the energy flow to the gravity control unit!

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.940
Beginning analysis of gravitational field.

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:41.630
Inverting output of exotic controller.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:50.660
Adding in Gluon controller.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:54.260
Tensor eigenvalues diverging.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:57.600
Turning gravity storm's energy upon itself.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.330
Eigenvalues converging. Inversion successful.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.330
Let's go!

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:10.160
Creating inverse gravitational field.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.840
Gravity control unit to maximum output!

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:36.860
It's started.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.940
Activating energy absorption.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.630
Defending with a nano-barrier.

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:05.850
The Gluon controller's processing speed cannot keep up with the gravitational field is changing!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.580
Keep at it!

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:09.860
I cannot endure any more than this!

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.740
No! Don't give up!

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.290
It's impossible to process any faster! It's at my limit!

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:18.860
Not yet!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.730
At this rate the ship shall collapse!

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.100
Have you forgotten? Survive until the very end!

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:52.880
Oh no!

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.860
The ship is...

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.030
Don't give up! Even if my body turns to dust!

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:05.060
Luna...

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.010
Live!

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.100
Luna!

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.230
The space ship has disappeared from the radar!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.060
But...

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:25.460
But it doesn't seem like they were able to destroy the gravity storm.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:28.120
Luna! Is Luna okay?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.100
That much...

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:33.560
Look at this!

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:38.340
The gravity storm's course has changed! It's moving away from the planet!

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:43.460
Can you hear me?

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:48.080
The gravity storm's course has changed! The operation was a success!

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.060
She did it.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:53.890
She saved the planet.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.490
And Luna...

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:09.600
Luna...

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:12.450
Luna.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:18.540
Dad!

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:19.650
Luna.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.380
Dad!

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:30.010
I guess I really did it.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:33.830
Yes, you accomplished everything.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:37.280
You saved the planet, and everyone's lives.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:38.810
Good.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:41.810
You've worked very hard, Luna.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:47.930
What's wrong?

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:53.590
All this time, I've wanted you to praise me, Dad.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:56.630
It's like that's why I kept trying so hard.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:58.880
When really...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.830
When really I was just a crybaby.

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:12.010
I guess. Even though you're only 14, it looks like what I said to you made you grow up very quickly.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.140
It's okay.

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:17.890
From now on, don't be so reckless.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:22.280
As long as you're careful with your life, I'll be happy.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:23.590
Okay.

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:26.810
Well, off I go.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.450
You should go back to where everyone is.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:32.450
Dad!

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:36.980
We can see each other again any time. Goodbye, Luna.

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:38.250
Dad!

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:42.600
Dad!

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:49.460
Have you regained consciousness, Luna?

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:52.800
Survive, was it you?

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.910
Was it you who let me see my father?

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.840
It was your heart that let you.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:05.060
When the nanomachines and your mysterious power became one...

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:09.410
...that power may have created a new world.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:11.250
A new world?

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:14.510
The limitless possibilities people have.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.650
I have changed my mind.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:20.480
I will entrust the planet's future to you people.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:26.780
Create a world where people and machines can cooperate and live in harmony with nature.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:28.430
Survive...

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:34.430
And with that, my duty is also complete.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.940
Luna!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.270
She did it!

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:28.950
Survive protected her with a nanomachine shield!

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.890
Everyone...

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:56.590
Those were the people of this planet.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.900
The fleet that had long wandered space as nomads...

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:05.290
...had long ago received the message that Adam's parents and their colleagues had sent...

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:10.460
...and had returned now, after 1000 years it was to have taken for the climate to return to normal.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:12.380
And thus...

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.190
You're really going?

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:17.330
Yes, although we're a little sad.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:20.060
I mean, we did finally get a space ship.

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:23.080
We have to go before the gravity storm disappears, after all.

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:24.710
But it's dangerous!

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:28.210
There's no guarantee you'll make it home to your colony!

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.340
But there's a chance.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:31.430
Exactly!

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:36.890
This space ship can just about perfectly control gravitational fields using Higgs Bosons.

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:39.600
It's certainly worth giving it a try.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:41.740
Adam, stay healthy.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:47.890
If we get back to our colony, we'll remember our experiences on this planet.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.900
And we'll make sure they learn from the mistakes your people made.

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:52.390
Everyone...

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:59.210
And I'll work hard to follow in my parents' footsteps.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:03.300
I'll work with everyone to protect this planet!

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:04.090
Yes!

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:13.950
Adam...

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:17.180
Take care of it.

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:19.880
To me?

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:22.470
But it's precious to you, isn't it?

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.600
That's why I'm giving it to you.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:26.210
Menori...

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:31.050
Between planets, peoples, and languages, music never changes.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.900
It reaches the hearts of all people.

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:38.550
Some day, it will be a bridge that links our planets together.

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:45.150
Menori! Thank you! I'll take good care of it!

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:53.330
Tako, you stay healthy too.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.390
Yes, you too, Chako.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.340
And everyone else too!

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:01.760
Well everyone, off we go!

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.790
So much happened.

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:16.540
So much it's hard to put it all in words.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:19.840
Come to think of it, in the end we never gave a name to this planet.

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:21.530
Sharla...

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.090
Planet...

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:30.190
...Survive! How about that?

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:34.290
That name fits it perfectly!

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:36.000
Survive!

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:38.290
It's a good name.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:39.380
It really is.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.550
Our second homeworld, Survive.

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:45.850
Goodbye, Survive.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.750
The gravity storm has come into view!

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.030
Everyone, take your seats!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.090
Here we go!

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:40.280
Are you well? Now I'm the pilot of a Mars shuttle.

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.650
When I'm nearby, I might be able to stop in.

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:47.180
We've reached our goals for the settlement of planet Albion.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:50.660
I'm hoping my next assignment will be Earth.

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:54.300
I've finally finished writing out our adventure!

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:57.450
Make sure you read it! It's really interesting!

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:01.130
I'm looking down on Saturn from Titan.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:06.790
And when I become a mechanic on a transport ship to Pegasus, I plan on seeing the hot Jupiter.

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:08.790
Sorry for being out of touch.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:11.100
It's busy work being my father's private secretary.

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:16.910
I want to become a commonwealth parliament member and open trade with Planet Survive.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:18.680
And I also want to see Adam.

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:21.260
Hey, doing well?

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:24.680
It's the great Howard, number one actor in the universe.

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:28.200
So hurry up and watch one of my movies already!

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.340
You haven't even watched one, have you?

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:33.490
Anyways, make sure you watch the next one.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:36.980
As usual.

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:49.390
You can finally take the helmet off.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:52.580
Chako!

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:56.060
The fruits of our labour have finally bloomed.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.900
That's good air!

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:14.360
It sure is!

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:15.330
Right?

00:22:46.430 --> 00:22:49.880
Dad... we've finally come this far.

00:22:51.040 --> 00:22:54.190
Keeping the Tree of Life growing is hard work...

00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:58.840
...but I'm working hard to make Earth like it originally was.

00:22:59.780 --> 00:23:05.290
Because I feel like this really is our homeworld.

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:09.340
Well, there's lots'a stuff to do today!

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:11.140
Let's get to work, Luna!

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:12.530
Alright!

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:14.250
Off to work!

00:24:57.200 --> 00:25:00.000
The End
